      "id": "sol.amc-12b-2011-p1.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The sums are \\(2+4+6=12\\) and \\(1+3+5=9,\\) so the expression equals \\(\\dfrac{12}{9}-\\dfrac{9}{12}=\\dfrac{4}{3}-\\dfrac{3}{4}.\\)\n\nOver a common denominator this is \\[ \\dfrac{16}{12}-\\dfrac{9}{12}=\\dfrac{7}{12}. \\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Add the terms in each numerator and denominator first",
        "The expression becomes \\(\\dfrac{12}{9}-\\dfrac{9}{12}\\)"
      ],
